{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary","kind":"proposition","title":"Torus-knot dictionary: leptons at $H_2$ vs mesons at $H_3$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-meson"],"cites":["references/jones1987","references/kashaev1997"],"tags":["lepton","meson","torus-knot","hecke-algebra","dictionary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.lepton_meson_crossing_match","text":"lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary\"></a><p><em>The lepton and meson mass towers are both indexed by torus knots <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2, n)</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 3, 5, 7, \\ldots</code> (odd primes). We establish the following correspondence:</em></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Generation</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code></th>\n<th>Lepton (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2</code>)</th>\n<th>Quark flavor (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3</code>)</th>\n<th>Meson (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q\\bar{q}</code>)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1st</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{e}</code> (electron)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u, d</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code> (pion)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2nd</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu</code> (muon)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{c}, s</code> (charm, strange)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> (kaon)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3rd</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code> (tau)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{t}, \\mathfrak{b}</code> (top, bottom)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta, \\phi</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><em>The lepton at generation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> is the closure of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1^{2k+1}</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2(q)</code>. The meson at the same generation is the Hopf-bound pair of quarks whose flavor content involves <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2, 2k+1)</code> crossing structure in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.7.1"}
